You are not allowed to take any medication that is intended only as an emergency measure or temporary treatment of your condition (e.g., pain relief).

You must use the following information in order to obtain hormone prescriptions from doctors:
1) The name of the physician you wish to see;
2) Your gender identity(s);
3) A description of what type of injection will be administered;
4) An indication of whether there may be side effects associated with taking this medicine;
5) If possible, provide details about the dose given per day;
6) Any other relevant medical conditions such as allergies, medications, etc.;
7) How often you want injections done;
8) Whether you have been on hormonal therapy before;
9) What kind of anesthesia you need if using oral administration;
10) When you plan to start receiving these injections;
11) Where do you live?
